t, touching the cloth along its whole length, down to the shin; a small dark brown leather pouch on the front of the right hip; Osric's Lantern, a small closed dark-iron lantern, unlit with no flame, hanging close against the back of the right hip. Stylized hand-painted look like the concept: a few big clean colour blocks and a few big folds that keep the concept's strong painted light and shadow (large deep dark crimson shadow planes in the folds of the habit, under the shoulder cape and the hood, under the sash and belt, inside the robe splits and on the inner faces of the panels; lit crimson on the ridges of the folds; the habit is never one flat evenly lit red), smooth surfaces, little small-scale detail, no stitching, no studs, no embroidery, no frayed edges, no dirt. No glow anywhere, no rim light. Colours: deep crimson #8E1F24 on the lit planes and about #4A0E12 in the shadow planes, white linen #EFE6D2, dark brown leather, blackened iron #2B2B30, black cuffs #141214, ember orange only as flat paint on the coal-pot slots.
